id: pm-web-8dk0
title: "Every public API route lacked rate limiting, leaving auth and write endpoints open to abuse and denial of service"
description: "CodeQL reported 161 open high-severity alerts on origin/main: 155 js/missing-rate-limiting across every router in src/routes plus the file-serving routes in src/app.ts, 2 js/missing-token-validation (CSRF), 1 js/tainted-format-string, 1 js/request-forgery, 1 js/polynomial-redos and 1 js/insufficient-password-hash. grep for rate/limit/throttle in src returned nothing and the Caddy reverse proxy declares no rate_limit, so the finding was real and unhandled at every layer: every route was unthrottled, including credential-checking auth routes. pm-web is a multi-tenant hosted service meant to carry thousands of concurrent users per project, so unthrottled auth and write routes are an abuse and availability risk, not a lint nit. This adds real per-route rate limiting (express-rate-limit) with distinct tiers keyed on the real client IP behind the proxy, a CSRF guard, and fixes for the format-string, request-forgery and ReDoS alerts."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-28T12:56:06.843Z"
